# Hyprland's autogenerated fallback config. Stoa ships hyprland.lua; the
# .conf path only ever reappears when Hyprland starts without a config
# and writes its own stub. When ~/.config/hypr/hyprland.conf is still a
# symlink from a pre-lua install, that write lands *through* the dangling
# link and recreates the file in here, where `stoa-sync`'s `git add -A`
# would happily commit it. Ignore it so the stub can never come back.
config/hypr/hyprland.conf
